Create `/root/menu.sh` that uses a POSIX `case` on the first argument (`$1`) so it runs without keyboard input. Choices: `1` prints `System info`, `2` prints `Disk space`, `0` prints `Bye`, anything else prints `Invalid`.

```bash
#!/bin/sh
case "$1" in
  1) echo "System info" ;;
  2) echo "Disk space" ;;
  0) echo "Bye" ;;
  *) echo "Invalid" ;;
esac
```

Run it:

```bash
sh /root/menu.sh 1
```

Create `/root/wordtype.sh` that classifies `$1` with `case` patterns: `???)` means three characters, `*.txt)` means a name ending in .txt, and `*)` is the fallback.

```bash
#!/bin/sh
case "$1" in
  ???)   echo "three characters" ;;
  *.txt) echo "a text file" ;;
  *)     echo "something else" ;;
esac
```

Run it:

```bash
sh /root/wordtype.sh abc
```
